WEBVTT

00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:52.466
I cannot thank you guys enough
for your remarkable efforts.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:58.400
I believe that if
it weren't for your help,

00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:02.003
Jibral Castle would not
be standing here today.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:07.326
And we have something
we would like to ask you to do.

00:02:09.366 --> 00:02:12.096
We've contacted
the neighboring nations in secrecy.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.273
And together we've had discussions
that have led to a secret alliance.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.733
Our combined forces are preparing
for an invasion of Grankingdom.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.100
- What?!
- What?!

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.500
We would very much like you guys
to take part in this invasion.

00:02:23.866 --> 00:02:28.966
Unfortunately, our technology is a far cry
from that of the Grankingdom's.

00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:33.066
If you'd fight with us...

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:34.800
With all due respect...

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.900
We are travelers.

00:02:37.566 --> 00:02:43.166
Although our desire to defeat Nene
is the same, we cannot act together.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.500
Why not? We just fought together
in the earlier battle.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.303
We are not soldiers.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:53.700
Right, but...

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.300
Then it cannot be helped.

00:02:58.066 --> 00:02:59.066
By the way...

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:01.733
We spoke of a reward earlier...

00:03:02.566 --> 00:03:04.966
About the viewing of
the Book of the Beginning...

00:03:06.433 --> 00:03:07.733
About that...

00:03:08.533 --> 00:03:13.333
OPERATION MARRIAGE PROPOSAL

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:15.533
A thief broke in?!

00:03:16.066 --> 00:03:16.726
Yes.

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:22.103
Somebody broke into the Royal Library
while we were engaged in battle.

00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:23.573
Was it stolen?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.800
No, actually...

00:03:28.166 --> 00:03:29.796
Oh, it's here.

00:03:34.533 --> 00:03:36.033
Pages are torn out.

00:03:37.266 --> 00:03:38.766
Two guards were knocked out...

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.700
And someone tore out the last seven pages
and made off with them.

00:03:44.733 --> 00:03:46.233
The last seven pages?

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.000
Any idea who did this?

00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:48.903
No.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:55.030
But the man who you guys captured during
the ghost disturbance broke out of his cell...

00:03:55.433 --> 00:03:58.773
And he was found dead
outside the castle.

00:04:00.233 --> 00:04:01.233
That guy...

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.900
Okay, let's go!

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:09.030
What does this mean, maro?
He wasn't behind the ghost hoax, maro?

00:04:09.066 --> 00:04:12.666
What?! Then there really
was a ghost after all?!

00:04:13.233 --> 00:04:14.403
Of course not.

00:04:14.633 --> 00:04:17.103
But I wonder if it means there was
somebody entirely different

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:18.673
behind all that ghost stuff.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.500
Maybe...

00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:24.833
Salinas stole a part of
the Book of the Beginning,

00:04:24.866 --> 00:04:27.866
but somebody took him out
to keep quiet?

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.070
That's what we are thinking.

00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:34.933
And we also think
the whole Grankingdom attack

00:04:34.966 --> 00:04:37.396
was to distract us
from their true objective.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.770
Come to think of it, they sure pulled out
of that battle quickly, didn't they?

00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:44.103
Then the real culprit is
Grankingdom after all?

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:47.533
What does that mean, maro?!
I don't get it at all, maro!

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:54.200
It just means the stolen last pages
were extremely important, right?!

00:04:56.766 --> 00:04:58.666
Good job picking up on that, Kluke.

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:04.370
Why? Why not just look at any copy of
the Book of the Beginning in a library?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.600
The Extra Seven...

00:05:08.633 --> 00:05:12.303
That's what the stolen
last seven pages are called.

00:05:12.666 --> 00:05:14.426
The Extra Seven?

00:05:15.166 --> 00:05:22.366
As you mentioned, there are many copies of
the Book of the Beginning in many libraries.

00:05:22.966 --> 00:05:24.026
However...

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:27.403
the final seven pages
found in this book

00:05:27.433 --> 00:05:32.573
are only included in the original
Book of the Beginning here in Jibral.

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:33.833
The original...

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:36.866
So this is the original
Book of the Beginning?

00:05:37.533 --> 00:05:42.873
It's believed that the final seven pages
were added sometime after it was written.

00:05:43.833 --> 00:05:45.973
What was written in it?

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.030
You read it, didn't you, Conrad?

00:05:48.466 --> 00:05:52.796
No. I can't read it as
it's written in ancient letters.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:57.630
However, it's said that the long line
of kings knew the content.

00:05:58.033 --> 00:05:59.803
And I don't know why,

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:05.473
but it was sealed here so the Extra Seven
would not leak to the outside.

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:10.426
However, we forgot about that
over the years.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.730
The Book of the Beginning
has stuff written in it

00:06:12.766 --> 00:06:16.126
about the legendary Shadow Wielders
we're looking for, right?

00:06:16.466 --> 00:06:18.726
Hey, wait.
The Seven Soldiers of Light...

00:06:19.066 --> 00:06:21.496
I wonder if it has something
to do with the Extra Seven.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.470
The Seven Soldiers of Light
were Shadow Wielders?!

00:06:24.833 --> 00:06:27.703
Uh, yeah.
That's what Zola said.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.200
I see...

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.470
If that's true, then the legends
about the Soldiers of Light

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:35.370
and the war between light and darkness
could be more than just stories.

00:06:35.733 --> 00:06:39.733
Either way, we can't read it
since it's not here.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.670
Let's stop thinking about it.

00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:44.703
So that's why Zola wanted to
read it so badly?

00:06:46.966 --> 00:06:48.766
What in the world is written in it?

00:06:56.533 --> 00:06:59.903
What the heck are
you guys thinking?!

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:04.073
It's outrageous to turn down
his Majesty's request!

00:07:04.666 --> 00:07:06.226
Bye, old man.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.970
Well...uhh...
I appreciate all your help.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.530
Is it really okay?

00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:13.626
Certainly.

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:17.326
Under normal circumstances,
we'd come along.

00:07:18.066 --> 00:07:21.766
But Jibral Knights are
part of the invasion force.

00:07:22.633 --> 00:07:23.633
I wish you good luck in battle.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.600
We'll take back the Extra Seven
with our own hands.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:30.500
Let us meet again at that time.

00:07:30.833 --> 00:07:32.533
Stay well, Conrad!

00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:37.303
Yeah. I'm looking forward to the next time
that we get to fight together, Shu.

00:07:38.533 --> 00:07:39.203
Right!

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.070
Maro?

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:55.696
Stay well!

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.830
You too! Goodbye!

00:07:59.866 --> 00:08:01.566
Thanks for everything.

00:08:04.566 --> 00:08:06.496
Do you want to become
a Knight Master yourself?

00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:09.596
Huh? No, I...

00:08:10.766 --> 00:08:12.866
Right then, I figured it out.

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:15.433
What I want to become is...

00:08:17.266 --> 00:08:18.996
That's right... I...

00:08:30.733 --> 00:08:33.773
Man, this is awesome!

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.403
No matter how far we travel,
there's more ocean!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.870
Of course! It's the ocean.

00:08:39.266 --> 00:08:41.596
What is it, boy?
Is this your first time on the ocean?

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.530
Yeah, it is.

00:08:43.733 --> 00:08:45.933
We're from Talta Village.

00:08:46.366 --> 00:08:50.126
I see. Then I guess it's only natural
you find the ocean so interesting!

00:08:50.433 --> 00:08:53.833
The ocean's great.
It's so vast.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.800
And it's full of adventures
for us to explore!

00:08:57.433 --> 00:09:01.773
The kraken in the Gul Ocean,
the cursed realm of the Crystal Sea,

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.570
the Siren's Cape,
the legends of mermaids...

00:09:04.766 --> 00:09:08.496
And the Realm of Fatal Collision
we'll be passing through...

00:09:09.033 --> 00:09:10.233
Realm of...

00:09:10.266 --> 00:09:11.266
Fatal Collision?

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.000
Right. That's what it's called
among us seafarers.

00:09:16.633 --> 00:09:21.903
There's a legend that says
when the ocean's calm like today,

00:09:21.933 --> 00:09:25.233
a fog appears and envelops
the boat all of a sudden,

00:09:25.266 --> 00:09:26.696
cutting visibility to nothing.

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:31.933
And once it's enshrouded in the fog,
the boat's engine stalls,

00:09:31.966 --> 00:09:34.426
it's swept off by ocean currents,
and it disappears.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.300
Then several days later,
the ship is discovered.

00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:42.073
But the crew...is all dead.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:48.100
The rumors say that it was a ghost
or it was a virus that wiped them out.

00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:49.933
But in actuality,

00:09:49.966 --> 00:09:54.196
it seems that the crew members
fell under a curse and fought each other.

00:09:58.666 --> 00:09:59.796
Just kidding.

00:09:59.833 --> 00:10:00.503
Huh?

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:03.603
Well, it is true that there's
a lot of fog in these waters.

00:10:03.866 --> 00:10:05.926
And there are many
shallow areas around here.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.370
So seafarers have to be really careful
or they could run aground or sink.

00:10:09.733 --> 00:10:12.333
The rumor probably started
as a cautionary tale.

00:10:12.866 --> 00:10:14.596
Then it's a lie?

00:10:15.066 --> 00:10:16.396
I don't know about that.

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:23.133
What, they're teasing us?!

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:24.700
Th-That's right.

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.026
There's no such thing
as ghosts or curses.

00:10:28.566 --> 00:10:29.996
I don't know about that.

00:10:30.033 --> 00:10:31.033
Cut it out!

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.370
Hey, that hurts!

00:10:36.566 --> 00:10:38.796
I'm telling you to cut it out!

00:10:39.133 --> 00:10:41.273
What did I do?

00:10:41.433 --> 00:10:43.173
Don't act like you're all innocent.

00:10:43.966 --> 00:10:45.496
Hey!

00:10:45.533 --> 00:10:47.073
We've got trouble, maro!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.200
I'm the one in trouble.

00:10:49.566 --> 00:10:50.666
Is something wrong?

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.830
There was a pair of underwear
behind that barrel, maro!

00:10:56.233 --> 00:10:56.903
Huh?

00:10:57.133 --> 00:10:58.603
Why underwear?

00:10:58.966 --> 00:11:00.226
Hey, give those back!

00:11:01.033 --> 00:11:03.073
Oh, my underwear!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.100
It's not yours!

00:11:08.166 --> 00:11:10.296
Give me just one minute.

00:11:10.466 --> 00:11:11.796
Ta da!

00:11:12.733 --> 00:11:13.733
You are...

00:11:13.766 --> 00:11:14.966
- Bouquet!
- Bouquet!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.370
Long time no see.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:18.630
Hey, what're you doing here?!

00:11:18.833 --> 00:11:20.903
I told you I wouldn't
let you get away.

00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:23.303
And I told you we wouldn't
take you with us.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:27.370
Don't be embarrassed.
Just be honest.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.330
I'm being honest.

00:11:29.366 --> 00:11:32.526
That's alright. I already know.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.700
Hey, are you listening at all?

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:40.230
That's enough talk for now.
It's been so long since I last saw you!

00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:42.196
Oh... Uh...

00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:43.503
Hey, you!

00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:47.596
Give it a rest!
It's clear he hates that!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:48.770
Why?

00:11:49.366 --> 00:11:52.366
Why?
Isn't it obvious?!

00:11:52.566 --> 00:11:53.566
Obvious?

00:11:54.633 --> 00:11:57.573
No matter how you look at it,
he doesn't seem to hate that, maro.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.370
Rather, he looks happyâ€”

00:11:59.766 --> 00:12:02.626
Anyway, get away from him!
That's rude!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.270
Oh, I get it.

00:12:06.533 --> 00:12:07.933
W-What?

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.130
You're jealous, right?

00:12:10.233 --> 00:12:10.903
Huh?

00:12:11.466 --> 00:12:14.496
You don't like it when
Shu and I get along, right?

00:12:14.633 --> 00:12:18.933
No way!
What do I care what Shu does?

00:12:19.233 --> 00:12:20.603
Then there's no problem, right?

00:12:21.166 --> 00:12:21.826
Shu!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.800
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:24.033 --> 00:12:26.373
If you don't like it,
come right out and say so!

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:29.000
Right, maro!
Let me touch those boobs, too!

00:12:29.033 --> 00:12:30.433
Uh...

00:12:30.466 --> 00:12:31.496
You don't like it, right?

00:12:31.533 --> 00:12:32.873
Uh, umm...

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.400
Hey, hey!

00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:38.703
I don't understand!
What are you to Shu anyway?!

00:12:38.733 --> 00:12:39.403
Huh?

00:12:39.933 --> 00:12:41.733
Just what's your
relationship with Shu?

00:12:42.266 --> 00:12:43.766
Well...

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.370
Are you guys dating?

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.070
Wow...

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:47.300
No way!

00:12:47.666 --> 00:12:49.226
Then leave us alone.

00:12:49.466 --> 00:12:52.966
You don't have the right
to stop us from getting along.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.530
What?!

00:12:54.833 --> 00:12:57.273
Say, you two...

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.900
- You shut up!
- You shut up!

00:12:59.933 --> 00:13:01.873
What're you guys doing there?

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:05.100
You...

00:13:12.166 --> 00:13:14.896
So you stowed away
on this ship, huh?

00:13:16.833 --> 00:13:21.333
We're not going off to play!
We should let her off this ship immediately.

00:13:21.866 --> 00:13:25.726
Aren't you being a bit too cold?
We're right in the middle of the ocean!

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.800
Where do we even let her off?

00:13:27.833 --> 00:13:29.603
We are going to be facing
some dangerous situations.

00:13:29.633 --> 00:13:33.373
It's inadvisable to take along
someone who can't fight!

00:13:33.733 --> 00:13:36.573
She's a Shadow Wielder as well!

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:38.770
I don't want to cart along
yet another fifth wheel.

00:13:39.233 --> 00:13:41.533
This is just going to cause more trouble,
and I don't want any part of it!

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:44.800
Who do you mean by fifth wheel?!

00:13:45.733 --> 00:13:47.273
Do I need to state the obvious?

00:13:47.666 --> 00:13:48.966
You!

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:50.800
Stop it!

00:13:50.833 --> 00:13:52.733
Don't fight over me!

00:13:52.833 --> 00:13:56.433
No matter how adorable I may be
or how nice a body I may have,

00:13:56.466 --> 00:13:59.326
you two shouldn't be
fighting each other!

00:14:01.833 --> 00:14:03.533
What's the plan, maro? Zola?

00:14:03.933 --> 00:14:08.233
It's what I said before.
This is up to Shu.

00:14:08.666 --> 00:14:10.026
Me?!

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:13.130
So...
What're you going to do?

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:16.700
Of course you'll let me
join you guys, right?

00:14:17.233 --> 00:14:18.733
Huh?
Um...

00:14:19.033 --> 00:14:21.433
Some "spice" is indispensable
for a journey.

00:14:22.066 --> 00:14:23.926
Huh? Huh?

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.000
What're you going to do?!

00:14:26.266 --> 00:14:28.396
Well...uhh...

00:14:28.733 --> 00:14:29.403
Maro?

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.000
What is it, Marumaro?

00:14:31.533 --> 00:14:32.703
Look at that, maro!

00:14:42.466 --> 00:14:43.126
It's fog.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.130
I can't see anything ahead, maro.

00:14:59.333 --> 00:15:00.903
What's the deal all of a sudden?

00:15:01.533 --> 00:15:05.433
No way...
Could it be that legend?!

00:15:06.066 --> 00:15:07.266
It couldn't be...

00:15:07.433 --> 00:15:08.973
It's the Realm of Fatal Collision!

00:15:11.066 --> 00:15:13.026
Guys!
Be careful!

00:15:13.166 --> 00:15:15.866
Be careful?! This is just...

00:15:18.233 --> 00:15:18.903
Huh?!

00:15:21.833 --> 00:15:23.333
Are you okay?!

00:15:24.533 --> 00:15:25.833
This isn't just fog.

00:15:26.366 --> 00:15:28.566
Don't breathe in the fog!
We'll be screwed, too.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:29.900
Got it!

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.100
But then...

00:15:32.366 --> 00:15:34.926
Hey, old man! Old man!

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:39.370
Is he drunk?

00:15:39.566 --> 00:15:40.226
Guys!

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:42.970
This is...

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.070
Zola.

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:49.900
It seems there's something in this fog
that stimulates the central nervous system.

00:15:50.733 --> 00:15:53.073
With this, it's like
you're drinking alcohol.

00:15:54.533 --> 00:15:55.533
Zola!

00:16:03.033 --> 00:16:04.373
M-Marumaro?!

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.500
What's wrong, Marumaro?!

00:16:09.966 --> 00:16:10.966
Marumaro!

00:16:11.266 --> 00:16:11.926
Ma...

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:16.130
I'm a friend of justice, maro.

00:16:16.266 --> 00:16:20.066
We...We're justice...
What's justice?

00:16:20.233 --> 00:16:22.003
The fog has gotten to him.

00:16:23.833 --> 00:16:28.303
Go, maro! Bam Bam Beam!

00:16:28.333 --> 00:16:30.503
Bam Bam Beam!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:36.000
Cut it out, Marumaro!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:39.670
Nice, Saber Tiger!
One more time, maro!

00:16:39.866 --> 00:16:41.566
You drunk!

00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:43.133
Hey, Jiro!

00:16:43.333 --> 00:16:44.633
At this...rate...

00:16:45.666 --> 00:16:46.326
Jiro!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.930
I'm not gloomy!

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.770
Oh yes you are!

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:55.870
Well, I'm actually a happy guy.

00:16:56.066 --> 00:16:57.196
Hey, Jiro!

00:16:57.233 --> 00:16:59.873
What? The fog's
gotten him too?!

00:17:00.066 --> 00:17:04.796
Go, maro!
Bam Bam Beam, part two!

00:17:04.833 --> 00:17:07.273
Bam Bam Beam, part two!

00:17:10.566 --> 00:17:11.866
- Yes, maro!
- Yay!

00:17:12.333 --> 00:17:14.803
What're you doing, you jerk?!

00:17:14.833 --> 00:17:17.573
Let's go, Minotaur.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:19.000
Let's play together, maro!

00:17:19.033 --> 00:17:20.373
Here ya go!

00:17:23.766 --> 00:17:26.426
Mino-chan Punch!

00:17:28.333 --> 00:17:30.433
Cut it out, you two!

00:17:33.733 --> 00:17:38.773
They're going to sink the whole ship
if I don't do something about it!

00:17:40.933 --> 00:17:43.003
We're the only
normal ones left, huh?

00:17:43.166 --> 00:17:45.296
In other words,
we can hold our alcohol?

00:17:45.466 --> 00:17:47.526
But this won't hold up forever.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.470
What's that vortex?!

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:04.770
This is bad! At this rate,
we'll get pulled right into that vortex!

00:18:10.233 --> 00:18:10.903
Kluke!

00:18:14.433 --> 00:18:15.973
Help me, Shu!

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:17.000
Damn it!

00:18:28.333 --> 00:18:31.073
Blue Dragon! We're going to
blow away that vortex!

00:18:33.566 --> 00:18:36.326
I feel...kinda...weird.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:41.070
Is this...a watermelon?

00:18:41.333 --> 00:18:42.003
Shu!

00:18:42.266 --> 00:18:42.926
Yeah?!

00:18:42.966 --> 00:18:44.496
Hang in there, Shu!

00:18:44.533 --> 00:18:48.673
No, I'm all there, so it's okay.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.530
Jeez!
Pull yourself together!

00:18:51.966 --> 00:18:54.196
Oh, right.
I've pulled myself together!

00:18:55.866 --> 00:18:57.266
Hurry!

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:59.000
You just wait, Kluke!

00:18:59.566 --> 00:19:01.996
Blue Dragon!
Shoot through that vortex!

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.230
What're you aiming at?!

00:19:16.066 --> 00:19:19.066
That's my business.

00:19:20.766 --> 00:19:23.126
Even Blue Dragon is out of it.
Damn!

00:19:23.166 --> 00:19:24.166
Shu!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.170
My vision's getting cloudy again.

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:28.600
I've got to hurry.

00:19:28.633 --> 00:19:29.303
Shu!

00:19:29.533 --> 00:19:31.833
Let's go one more time,
Blue Dragon!

00:19:31.866 --> 00:19:33.326
Shut up, Shu.

00:19:34.033 --> 00:19:35.303
Blue Dragon?!

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:38.530
Let's just kick back and relax!

00:19:40.966 --> 00:19:42.126
This isn't working.

00:19:42.633 --> 00:19:44.503
Fine! Guess it's come to this.

00:19:46.833 --> 00:19:49.103
I'm Hippopotamus, hippo.

00:19:55.633 --> 00:19:57.773
Help me quick!

00:19:58.666 --> 00:20:01.066
I kinda wish I didn't come out.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.570
This is the moment of truth!

00:20:03.933 --> 00:20:04.603
Huh?

00:20:05.133 --> 00:20:07.533
We're going to prove
that we're useful.

00:20:07.866 --> 00:20:10.396
Oh, right.
I'll do my best!

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.400
Hipopon, Hipotama, Transform!

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.170
Hippo! Transform.

00:20:18.733 --> 00:20:19.403
There!

00:20:19.833 --> 00:20:20.933
A fan?

00:20:21.333 --> 00:20:23.633
First I'll blow away the fog.

00:20:24.166 --> 00:20:26.026
I get it! Blue Dragon!

00:20:26.333 --> 00:20:28.433
It's up to you, Shu!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.000
I know!

00:20:30.366 --> 00:20:32.066
I can't hang on any longer!

00:20:37.600 --> 00:20:39.570
Alright. We can do this, Shu!

00:20:54.933 --> 00:20:57.673
Alright! My head's
starting to clear up too!

00:21:01.133 --> 00:21:04.603
That's the creature behind this!
Let's go, Blue Dragon!

00:21:12.133 --> 00:21:13.673
What?

00:21:16.266 --> 00:21:17.266
What's that?

00:21:20.200 --> 00:21:22.370
You're an eyesore!

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:25.370
Jeez...

00:21:29.966 --> 00:21:32.226
What? What was I doing?

00:21:32.633 --> 00:21:33.633
Maro.

00:21:38.466 --> 00:21:40.326
Why's the mast busted?

00:21:40.366 --> 00:21:41.026
Who knows?

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.430
I thought I was going to die.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.800
What the heck was I doing, maro?

00:21:46.666 --> 00:21:48.066
I don't remember at all.

00:21:48.766 --> 00:21:52.026
At the end of the day,
Bouquet saved us, huh?

00:21:52.533 --> 00:21:54.773
I guess she wasn't
a fifth wheel after all, maro.

00:21:55.166 --> 00:21:56.166
I acknowledge that.

00:21:56.366 --> 00:21:58.026
What happened
to those two, maro?

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:58.970
Huh?

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:02.870
I don't feel good.
I still feel a little woozy.

00:22:03.533 --> 00:22:05.403
So, Shu?

00:22:05.733 --> 00:22:08.433
Now you know that
I can be of use, right?

00:22:08.833 --> 00:22:11.533
Yeah, yeah...
We all would've been lost without you.

00:22:11.833 --> 00:22:13.703
So it's okay if I came along?

00:22:14.033 --> 00:22:17.433
Yeah, sure... I doubt anybody's
going to complain now.

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:20.170
Then, marry me.

00:22:20.333 --> 00:22:22.333
Yeah sure.
Hey, what was that?!

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:24.000
I'm so glad!

00:22:24.666 --> 00:22:27.026
Jeez!
Cut it out!

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:30.600
We're engaged!
Lucky, Wiki, Monkikki!

00:22:30.633 --> 00:22:32.773
Cut it out! Cut it out!

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:35.630
Hey, what're you doing?!

00:22:35.733 --> 00:22:38.373
Huh? Kluke, this isn't...

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:39.930
This isn't what?!

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:44.000
Oh! The fog again!
I'm going to sleep.

00:22:44.233 --> 00:22:46.933
Don't lie!

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:23.570
Shu's party has infiltrated
the Grankingdom,

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.830
but they are separated
from each other by Logi.

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:28.170
Are you okay, Marumaro?

00:24:28.200 --> 00:24:32.230
Jiro's fighting a girl but my opponent
is an old man wearing glasses!

00:24:32.266 --> 00:24:33.696
There's no motivation, maro.

00:24:33.733 --> 00:24:35.273
My opponent is an old man
with his hair slicked back

00:24:35.300 --> 00:24:36.730
and he has an angry look
in his eyes.

00:24:36.766 --> 00:24:37.766
Wait, that's Logi!

00:24:37.800 --> 00:24:40.230
Next time on Blue Dragon:
"Logi Strikes."
